ative":"Employs approximately 635 people. Revenue per employee of $563K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $136K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["WILSON BANK HOLDING CO is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.8B market cap on $357M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $86M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 206% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.0605393248876847},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.5pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jack W. Bell buys 671 shares of Wilson Bank Holding Co (WBHC) at $85 each. - Stock Titan","source":"Stock Titan","link":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxPTzFpWEQ0Wml0YkhvSGE0Z2tRMnRSaV9WbEdQWlo2a1FnUmdGVklpSnYyNEtwajZ1RUJMUG51RHBDNmxVd0UyV0NGampUUEFfSUQ0eDNSb2p5U1ZFZ01kNnFvbTVRZXk4YTZBRnhza1M1b1FOZXo4Z2o1ejNUc1pKYlVyam5NLWkwcGtqVEtWeTVsSmNrRVYzNDcwMzFvYkdUMFROeG9lS1pWSHdRM21vMG9uYWZ5MG8?oc=5","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795447492.0,"origin":"google_news_ticker","tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"After gifting 671 shares, Jack W. Bell reported holding 178,230 shares directly in Wilson Bank Holding Co (WBHC). - Stock Titan","source":"Stock Titan","link":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQTjlqdlF5bUFHYlR5SklVY0Q4TXBDYWUwM3k1NWk0MHE0Z3ZhUzVqcVRDNnl0aE9XeFJkMnVvVWFBWmtGX1lTWXlTdVRNSW81T2ZKemtNOXNmN3ljb0IzSGlYMjhUNEd6R0lQT